WEBVTT

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:05.330
Welcome!

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.580
Could I get a cooling hat?

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.920
Thank you.

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:10.580
I'll take your measurements.

00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:14.880
There...

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:16.130
Excuse me, but I'd like to return these.

00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:18.040
I'll handle that right away!

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:19.750
One, two, three,

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:22.380
Business sure is booming.
four, five, six, seven, eight...<b></b>

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:24.880
The number of gatherers around
had really dropped off for a while,

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:27.080
but they actually seem to be on the rise lately!

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:28.500
Yes, fortunately.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:32.540
There is of course the cooling hats,
and then there's the sale of

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:36.920
the frostfang bat and hellflame grizzly
ingredients to South Straug.

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:39.830
And we've had requests
to buy ingredients too.

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:42.920
Good going there, Sarasa!

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:46.790
Ms. Sarasa's desire to bring
prosperity to the entire village

00:00:46.790 --> 00:00:49.630
is coming together, bit by bit.

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:52.960
Yeah, I guess you could say
we've taken our first big step.

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:58.460
Then we've gotta get fired up and
gather some good ingredients ourselves!

00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:01.540
In that case,

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:08.670
I'd appreciate you hurrying up and leaving
rather than dawdling around here forever!

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:11.960
Ah, it's just so cool and comfortable here that...

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:13.170
Ms. Owner!

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:17.210
We've brought information about
a real valuable ingredient!

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:21.540
You can supposedly gather
marsen clams near Yok Village!

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:23.750
Marsen clams?

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:35.790
Kyou kara mieru yo chiisai hoshi

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:39.210
Terashitete ne mune no naka o

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:42.500
Naite waratte kagaiyaite

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:44.750
Udemakutte arukidasou

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:47.960
(Kitto alright nayamu wa go sign)

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:50.210
(Kichin to yarimashou)

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:57.580
Jiyuu sugiru tte nante fujiyuu nan deshou

00:01:57.580 --> 00:02:00.920
Datte tokenai no yo

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:04.330
Rironchi jikkenchi spiral

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:06.420
Maido utedo katte mo

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:08.000
(Nani o tameshite mite mo)

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:09.670
Nengan kanatte shikuhakku

00:02:09.670 --> 00:02:11.500
(Cheat ja nai yo life hack)

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:14.960
Harete ippo fumidaseru license

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:17.210
Kore kara ga hajimari

00:02:17.380 --> 00:02:21.460
Kyou kara mieru yo chiisai hoshi

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:24.830
Terashitete ne mune no naka o

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:28.250
Naite waratte kagaiyaite

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:30.830
Shigoto no mae wa shinkokyuu

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:35.000
Hibike te o nobashita shintenchi

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:38.330
Yume wa kitto te no naka

00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:41.750
Kitto dekiru original

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:44.460
Door o akete welcome de ikou

00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:46.960
(Sore ja koko ga start)

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:50.460
(Kitto alright nayamu wa go sign)

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:52.880
(Kichin to yarimashou)

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:59.710
A gatherer we know apparently gathered
a whole lot of marsen clams

00:02:59.710 --> 00:03:03.580
at the lake in the forest
to the southeast of the village!

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:07.080
You're supposed to be able to get a real valuable
ingredient out of those bivalves, right?

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:13.080
If we gather a whole lot, we may even
be able to handle our debt all in one go!

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:13.330
<b>Freedom</b>

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:15.790
That might be a bit of an exaggeration,

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:18.750
but I'd imagine we'll be able to do
a good bit to pay you back.

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:23.750
If things go well, they could even become
a local specialty for the village, so...

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:25.500
Hmm...

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:26.790
Huh?

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:29.830
<b>Hmm...</b>

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:29.830
You... don't seem especially interested.

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:33.290
The only part of a marsen clam that can
be used as an alchemic ingredient

00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:35.580
is the gonads from the females.

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:40.130
It's difficult for amateurs to tell the males
and females apart just by looking,

00:03:40.130 --> 00:03:42.210
which makes it inefficient to gather them.

00:03:42.210 --> 00:03:45.630
To be blunt, I can't recommend it!

00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:47.330
Is that so...?

00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:51.630
I really thought we had something...

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:54.670
P-please don't get so down about it!

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:58.130
I'm a bit interested in marsen clams too.

00:03:58.130 --> 00:03:59.080
Huh?

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:05.380
There's a recipe using them in the book
from your master, Ms. Sarasa.

00:04:06.250 --> 00:04:10.750
I've wanted to make it for a while...

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:12.880
but we can't, right?

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:17.040
Alright, let's go get some!

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:17.790
Huh?!

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:18.880
Yay!

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:22.670
What, even though our proposal
was shot down immediately...?

00:04:22.670 --> 00:04:24.710
Ms. Owner is partial to Lorea!

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:30.290
Well, I want to eat Lorea's cooking...

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:36.040
At any rate, let's all head out
to the lake in the forest!

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:37.540
Yeah!

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:44.290
Is it alright, closing up shop?

00:04:44.290 --> 00:04:45.170
Yes.

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:49.170
I put up a notice of the temporary closure,

00:04:49.170 --> 00:04:52.880
and I entrusted Mr. Darna's
general store with potions

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:55.540
that may be needed in case of emergency.

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:57.250
I see.

00:04:57.250 --> 00:05:00.170
In that case, there's no need to
worry about gatherers getting injured.

00:05:00.170 --> 00:05:02.330
Alright, let us be off!

00:05:03.460 --> 00:05:06.630
That's quite the big box, Lorea...

00:05:07.210 --> 00:05:08.960
Do you want me to carry it?

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:10.750
You can put it in my backpack.

00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:12.500
Thank you.

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:15.880
But... I want to carry this myself.

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:18.540
Oh, really?

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:19.830
Got it.

00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:23.460
Just let me know if you get tired,
and I can take it for you whenever.

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:24.500
Right!

00:05:26.710 --> 00:05:32.630
I'd like for today to be a nice refreshing day
for Lorea, Ms. Kate, and Ms. Iris,

00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:36.420
since they're always helping out with the shop.

00:05:41.330 --> 00:05:47.250
Still, why don't the people of Yok Village
visit the lake if there's one so nearby?

00:05:47.250 --> 00:05:48.500
Hmm...

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:51.130
Well, if I had to say...

00:05:51.130 --> 00:05:56.920
Nobody can really swim there,
and you can't catch many fish either.

00:05:56.920 --> 00:06:00.380
Also, you get a lot of monsters
popping up in the forest, so...

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:02.330
Th-there they are!

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:07.210
S-splendidly done!

00:06:07.460 --> 00:06:09.960
It's true that if you treated it like a picnic
and let your guard down,

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:11.460
you could end up dead in a flash...

00:06:11.460 --> 00:06:12.960
R-right.

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:18.170
Is that the lake?

00:06:18.170 --> 00:06:19.790
No, that's...

00:06:25.210 --> 00:06:26.460
So pretty...!

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:28.630
Right, there was a place like this on the way.

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:31.000
Ah, look!

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:33.420
This one's really cute!

00:06:34.170 --> 00:06:38.170
You certainly are a young maiden,
Lorea, calling a flower cute.

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:40.750
Uwah!

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:43.500
Are you alright, Ms. Iris?!

00:06:43.750 --> 00:06:46.540
Are bugs... cute?
Huh?! Your nose?! That little guy got it?!<b></b>

00:06:46.540 --> 00:06:48.000
Lorea certainly has some interesting tastes.
Huh?! Your nose?! That little guy got it?!<b></b>

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:49.380
Lorea certainly has some interesting tastes.
Oh no!<b></b>

00:06:52.380 --> 00:06:55.790
Those potions I brought along
just in case sure did come in handy.

00:06:55.790 --> 00:06:58.210
My apologies, Ms. Owner...

00:06:58.460 --> 00:07:00.040
Look everybody!

00:07:01.170 --> 00:07:02.750
It's come into view!

00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:05.380
Now then!

00:07:05.380 --> 00:07:06.580
Right to it!

00:07:07.710 --> 00:07:09.420
It's gathering time!

00:07:09.580 --> 00:07:12.710
<b>Gurgle...</b>

00:07:09.580 --> 00:07:12.710
<b>Gurgle...</b>

00:07:12.920 --> 00:07:16.380
Ms. Iris, Ms. Kate!

00:07:16.630 --> 00:07:18.920
Don't you think it's about time for lunch?

00:07:18.920 --> 00:07:21.080
I brought one along for everyone!

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:27.420
Looks delicious!

00:07:27.630 --> 00:07:29.170
I brought tea too.

00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:31.290
Please, dig in!

00:07:31.290 --> 00:07:33.290
Let's eat!

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:36.000
So good!

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:37.250
Tasty!

00:07:39.420 --> 00:07:44.080
So it was this lunch that Lorea
took such care to bring along.

00:07:44.420 --> 00:07:46.330
She brought along so much...

00:07:46.330 --> 00:07:49.790
It must have been tough making it,
and carrying it all too.

00:07:50.330 --> 00:07:53.500
I'm so glad everyone's enjoying it!

00:07:57.920 --> 00:07:59.170
Hey...!

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:00.830
So cute!

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:03.460
It must be a small animal
that lives in the area.

00:08:03.630 --> 00:08:06.750
Do you want to eat Lorea's lunch too?

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:10.290
Here, as a special treat.

00:08:14.290 --> 00:08:16.500
Is it asking for seconds?

00:08:16.500 --> 00:08:19.130
It seems to have taken
a liking to you, Ms. Sarasa.

00:08:26.330 --> 00:08:28.000
Thanks for the meal.

00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:32.710
Now that my belly is full,
perhaps it's time for a midday nap!

00:08:36.210 --> 00:08:38.580
That's not what you meant to say, right, Iris?

00:08:38.750 --> 00:08:41.500
Next time, I might just get your face instead!

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:44.380
I-I-I was just joking, really!

00:08:44.380 --> 00:08:47.830
Alright, let's go gather some marsen clams!

00:08:47.830 --> 00:08:48.920
Ah, hold on!

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:51.710
You're going to dive dressed like that?

00:08:51.710 --> 00:08:53.330
Oh, right...!

00:08:57.460 --> 00:09:01.170
Let's go gather some marsen clams!

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:07.330
Good luck!

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:21.420
We got some!

00:09:21.420 --> 00:09:24.170
Looks like we can gather a whole lot,
just like we heard!

00:09:24.170 --> 00:09:25.420
That's amazing!

00:09:25.420 --> 00:09:27.290
Give it your all, you two!

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:28.210
Right!

00:09:36.540 --> 00:09:38.130
Hey, Ms. Sarasa...

00:09:38.130 --> 00:09:39.880
What is it, Lorea?

00:09:39.880 --> 00:09:43.130
You can gather jewels from
marsen clams, can't you?

00:09:43.130 --> 00:09:45.170
What sort are they?!

00:09:45.170 --> 00:09:47.500
I figure it'd be more accurate
to say you can make them.

00:09:47.500 --> 00:09:49.630
Just marsen clams aren't enough
on their own, though.

00:09:49.630 --> 00:09:50.540
Huh?!

00:09:50.540 --> 00:09:54.750
You need other ingredients and
proper training to make a jewel.

00:09:54.750 --> 00:09:57.830
And those ingredients are all
a bit expensive too...

00:09:59.330 --> 00:10:05.130
Still, I never knew that you could
make jewelry too using alchemy.

00:10:05.130 --> 00:10:10.330
I suppose rather than jewelry, you'd generally
talk about ingredients for artifacts.

00:10:10.330 --> 00:10:13.920
For example, take this artifact pendant.

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:18.210
The jewel in it was used making alchemy.

00:10:18.210 --> 00:10:22.580
It's a lot more expensive than what you
can make with marsen clams, though.

00:10:22.790 --> 00:10:26.170
Wow, is that so?!

00:10:26.170 --> 00:10:27.670
Hey!

00:10:28.040 --> 00:10:30.170
I gathered those!

00:10:30.170 --> 00:10:32.130
Victory goes to the swift!

00:10:33.130 --> 00:10:35.040
The two of them certainly seem
to be in high spirits.

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:39.210
It must be fun swimming like that.

00:10:39.210 --> 00:10:42.420
Then do you want to try
swimming together, Lorea?

00:10:42.420 --> 00:10:43.460
Huh?!

00:10:46.380 --> 00:10:49.790
This is my first time ever wearing a swimsuit!

00:10:50.170 --> 00:10:54.460
I thought maybe you'd like to swim too,
so I brought it along just to be safe.

00:10:54.460 --> 00:10:56.540
Let's hurry on into the water.

00:10:56.540 --> 00:10:57.960
R-right!

00:10:59.920 --> 00:11:02.540
Nice and slow, bit by bit...

00:11:04.420 --> 00:11:05.580
So chilly!

00:11:06.540 --> 00:11:08.290
You'll get used to it soon.

00:11:11.710 --> 00:11:13.960
Don't rush.
Just take your time practicing.

00:11:13.960 --> 00:11:17.210
For now, let's make learning to
flutter kick your goal for today!

00:11:17.210 --> 00:11:18.210
Right!

00:11:19.330 --> 00:11:21.290
One, two, one, two...

00:11:21.290 --> 00:11:23.580
Come on, you've got to move those legs.

00:11:25.040 --> 00:11:27.670
Please don't let go!

00:11:27.670 --> 00:11:29.210
Don't worry.

00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:32.290
Just look down at the bottom of the lake
and stretch out your legs.

00:11:32.290 --> 00:11:34.000
And don't bend your knees.

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:35.380
R-right.

00:11:41.210 --> 00:11:43.130
C-calm down, Lorea!

00:11:43.130 --> 00:11:44.460
Stop panicking!

00:11:50.420 --> 00:11:51.670
Lorea...

00:11:52.380 --> 00:11:55.250
Why don't you give this a try?

00:11:58.000 --> 00:12:00.330
I'm floating! My whole body is!

00:12:00.330 --> 00:12:01.830
What is this thing?!

00:12:01.830 --> 00:12:06.290
I made it using the scraps from
the ingredients for the magic stoves.

00:12:06.290 --> 00:12:08.540
Huh?! Really?!

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:12.130
I figured it could serve as a rescue tool
if Ms. Iris and Ms. Kate

00:12:12.130 --> 00:12:14.380
ran into trouble out in the water.

00:12:14.380 --> 00:12:17.380
You're always so perfectly prepared, Ms. Sarasa!

00:12:17.380 --> 00:12:20.960
I might just be able to concentrate on
moving my legs thanks to this!

00:12:23.330 --> 00:12:24.290
Like this...

00:12:24.290 --> 00:12:26.830
Try kicking with the tops of your feet.

00:12:27.210 --> 00:12:29.040
Get in a one, two rhythm.

00:12:29.040 --> 00:12:30.380
R-right!

00:12:30.790 --> 00:12:33.630
One, two, one, two, one, two...

00:12:33.630 --> 00:12:35.540
That's the way, you're doing great!

00:12:36.750 --> 00:12:39.630
One, two, one, two, one, two...

00:12:47.000 --> 00:12:49.420
Aren't you getting tired, Lorea?

00:12:49.420 --> 00:12:51.130
Why not take a bit of a break?

00:12:51.130 --> 00:12:53.170
No, I'm fine!

00:12:53.170 --> 00:12:56.460
I get the feeling that
I'll get the knack of it soon.

00:12:57.210 --> 00:12:58.830
Lorea's amazing...

00:12:59.460 --> 00:13:01.080
Thinking back, just recently...

00:13:02.830 --> 00:13:04.420
What's wrong, Lorea?!

00:13:05.250 --> 00:13:07.040
I'm so sorry, Ms. Sarasa!

00:13:07.040 --> 00:13:09.380
I wasted all these ingredients.

00:13:09.380 --> 00:13:11.170
Don't worry about that!

00:13:11.170 --> 00:13:12.880
You didn't get burned, did you?!

00:13:12.880 --> 00:13:15.830
No, that's not an issue.

00:13:16.290 --> 00:13:18.920
Still, just where did I mess up...?

00:13:18.920 --> 00:13:21.750
I was looking at the book
and everything when I made them...

00:13:23.380 --> 00:13:26.920
Ah, sorry! This is my fault!

00:13:26.920 --> 00:13:27.750
Huh?

00:13:27.750 --> 00:13:32.080
The settings and temperature scale
for a magic oven

00:13:32.080 --> 00:13:35.000
are pretty different than
with an ordinary one.

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:39.750
If you set this to around one fourth
of the strength listed in the book,

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:41.880
it should work out well.

00:13:41.880 --> 00:13:46.330
Um, do you mind if I try remaking them...?

00:13:47.540 --> 00:13:50.250
Of course not!
Try as many times as you want!

00:13:51.210 --> 00:13:52.920
Thank you!

00:13:52.920 --> 00:13:55.130
I'll keep on trying
till they come out delicious!

00:13:56.580 --> 00:13:57.670
Ah!

00:13:57.920 --> 00:13:59.580
Undercooked!

00:13:59.580 --> 00:14:01.580
They're all over the place!

00:14:01.830 --> 00:14:04.460
It turned into something else entirely!

00:14:04.460 --> 00:14:06.500
Geez!

00:14:06.710 --> 00:14:09.500
Even so, Lorea kept on giving her all.

00:14:12.130 --> 00:14:14.080
Ms. Sarasa!

00:14:14.330 --> 00:14:16.330
I finally did it!

00:14:20.130 --> 00:14:21.380
Delicious!

00:14:21.380 --> 00:14:22.710
You really mean it?!

00:14:22.710 --> 00:14:24.880
Yeah, they're really good!

00:14:24.880 --> 00:14:28.130
They may just be even better than the cookies
from sweet shops in the capital!

00:14:29.210 --> 00:14:31.170
Thank goodness!

00:14:32.330 --> 00:14:33.080
Though she looks all warm and snuggly,

00:14:33.080 --> 00:14:34.710
I'm so glad!
Though she looks all warm and snuggly,<b></b>

00:14:34.710 --> 00:14:36.880
once she sets her mind on something,

00:14:36.880 --> 00:14:39.290
Lorea keeps on trying really hard
till the very end.

00:14:41.830 --> 00:14:44.630
I love that about her...

00:14:45.170 --> 00:14:46.380
Ms. Sarasa!

00:14:48.670 --> 00:14:51.460
Please stay right where you are.

00:14:51.710 --> 00:14:52.710
Huh?

00:14:52.830 --> 00:14:54.960
I'm going to swim on over to you!

00:14:57.330 --> 00:14:58.830
Huh?! Lorea...?

00:15:00.630 --> 00:15:01.960
Lorea...

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:04.040
Give it your all!

00:15:04.040 --> 00:15:06.170
Let's go, let's go, Lorea!

00:15:07.750 --> 00:15:10.580
That's the way! Just a little more!

00:15:18.420 --> 00:15:20.040
You made it!

00:15:20.210 --> 00:15:22.460
You're amazing, Lorea!

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:25.960
I-it was just a bit, but I swam!

00:15:25.960 --> 00:15:27.920
I swam for the first time ever!

00:15:27.920 --> 00:15:28.750
Yeah!

00:15:28.750 --> 00:15:31.040
Once you get breathing and
how to move your arms down,

00:15:31.040 --> 00:15:33.080
you'll be able to swim even more!

00:15:33.080 --> 00:15:35.420
You really are amazing!
Such a quick learner!

00:15:35.420 --> 00:15:39.920
Oh no... It's all because
you're such a good teacher.

00:15:41.330 --> 00:15:45.380
Lorea, let's come here again to practice more.

00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:46.460
Right!

00:15:47.130 --> 00:15:50.000
I'm counting on you, Teach!

00:15:56.000 --> 00:15:57.630
We got quite a haul.

00:15:57.630 --> 00:15:58.750
Indeed!

00:15:58.750 --> 00:16:00.960
This much should be plenty,
don't you think?

00:16:01.380 --> 00:16:03.790
Ms. Kate! Ms. Iris!

00:16:04.790 --> 00:16:08.750
It's getting dark, so don't you think
it's about time to get out?!

00:16:08.750 --> 00:16:12.080
Yes, we were getting ready to do just that!

00:16:12.080 --> 00:16:14.080
We'll hurry back over your way!

00:16:15.420 --> 00:16:16.420
Watch out, you two!

00:16:16.420 --> 00:16:17.750
Behind you!

00:16:43.250 --> 00:16:46.040
What even is that giant slithery thing?!

00:16:47.080 --> 00:16:49.420
What is that, Ms. Sarasa?!

00:16:49.420 --> 00:16:51.250
That's a ligarex.

00:16:51.250 --> 00:16:52.460
A ligarex?

00:16:52.710 --> 00:16:55.210
It's my first time seeing one too.

00:16:55.830 --> 00:16:58.000
Hey, Ms. Owner!

00:16:58.250 --> 00:16:59.330
Ms. Kate! Ms. Iris!

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:01.380
Something unbelievable
sure did pop up, huh?

00:17:01.380 --> 00:17:04.130
I'll drive it away!

00:17:15.920 --> 00:17:17.750
After we went and gathered all those!

00:17:17.750 --> 00:17:18.420
Unforgivable, you wriggly fiend!

00:17:18.420 --> 00:17:19.630
Where'd that come from?!
Unforgivable, you wriggly fiend!<b></b>

00:17:19.630 --> 00:17:20.630
Unforgivable, you wriggly fiend!

00:17:20.830 --> 00:17:22.830
Take this! And this!

00:17:22.830 --> 00:17:24.040
And a little of this!

00:17:24.920 --> 00:17:26.380
What's this?!

00:17:31.750 --> 00:17:34.670
The surface of its body is so slimy
that swords won't work on it!

00:17:35.290 --> 00:17:36.580
How impudent!

00:17:39.880 --> 00:17:41.380
If I can't slash it, I'll stab!

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:44.540
Ah, watch out!

00:17:44.540 --> 00:17:45.580
Ligarexes...

00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:47.460
Huh?

00:17:50.130 --> 00:17:51.750
They give off electricity!

00:17:51.750 --> 00:17:53.830
You should've told me sooner...!

00:18:00.790 --> 00:18:01.670
Kate!

00:18:01.670 --> 00:18:02.790
Are you okay?

00:18:02.790 --> 00:18:04.210
Let's hurry to shore...

00:18:08.170 --> 00:18:09.420
Kate!

00:18:14.210 --> 00:18:15.210
Kate!
Ms. Kate!<b></b>

00:18:15.210 --> 00:18:16.710
Ice needle!

00:18:19.250 --> 00:18:20.460
Ms. Owner!

00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:23.580
Ms. Iris, I froze it using magic!

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:25.630
Let's take it down now, while we have a...

00:18:32.380 --> 00:18:34.130
It's time I get serious too!

00:18:34.460 --> 00:18:35.830
Force bullet!

00:18:42.130 --> 00:18:44.330
Time to finish this!

00:18:48.130 --> 00:18:49.540
Air blast!

00:18:57.330 --> 00:18:58.630
What is that...?

00:19:05.330 --> 00:19:07.080
A-amazing...

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:10.210
Now I've done it...

00:19:16.000 --> 00:19:18.960
Sorry for surprising you all...

00:19:18.960 --> 00:19:20.080
Ms. Sarasa...?

00:19:20.080 --> 00:19:21.670
What was that magic?

00:19:21.670 --> 00:19:25.000
Normally, this pendant keeps things in check.

00:19:25.250 --> 00:19:30.330
I have a bit more magical power than most,
and it has a tendency to run wild...

00:19:30.580 --> 00:19:32.080
You call that just a little...?

00:19:32.080 --> 00:19:35.040
I'm just glad that none of you got hurt.

00:19:35.250 --> 00:19:40.420
It was a bit of a surprise, but as a result
you saved our lives once again.

00:19:40.420 --> 00:19:41.960
Thank you.

00:19:41.960 --> 00:19:43.710
And just look!

00:19:44.460 --> 00:19:46.130
See, over there!

00:19:47.250 --> 00:19:49.290
A huge haul of marsen clams!

00:19:49.540 --> 00:19:52.670
That tornado from before
must have pulled them all up!

00:19:52.670 --> 00:19:54.040
We can take as many as we can carry!

00:19:56.540 --> 00:19:58.130
Everyone!

00:19:58.790 --> 00:20:02.920
Why don't we go ahead and try them fresh,
since we have the opportunity?

00:20:13.290 --> 00:20:17.130
Girl, girl, boy, boy, girl, girl!

00:20:23.960 --> 00:20:25.130
Delicious!

00:20:25.130 --> 00:20:27.880
The broiled ligarex is tasty too!

00:20:28.130 --> 00:20:30.790
This marsen clam chowder is fantastic!

00:20:30.790 --> 00:20:32.000
You mean it?

00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:32.790
Yeah!

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:35.290
I can feel it warming up my chilled body.

00:20:36.210 --> 00:20:37.210
Seconds!

00:20:37.210 --> 00:20:39.330
So quick! But me too...

00:20:39.540 --> 00:20:40.830
On it!

00:20:59.080 --> 00:21:00.880
What a beautiful melody.

00:21:00.880 --> 00:21:02.210
What song is it?

00:21:02.210 --> 00:21:04.460
It's one passed down in Yok Village.

00:21:04.460 --> 00:21:06.830
I just suddenly wanted to sing it...

00:21:50.250 --> 00:21:53.540
I had intended for today to help
Lorea and everyone relax...

00:21:54.170 --> 00:21:57.170
But in the end, I was the one
who was soothed more than anyone!

00:22:24.500 --> 00:22:30.210
Mado kara fuwari sashikomu hizashi

00:22:30.500 --> 00:22:36.000
Mezame no yokan ga sasayakikakeru

00:22:36.420 --> 00:22:42.040
Kitai to sukoshi no yuuki tsurete

00:22:42.420 --> 00:22:47.580
Seichou no kakera sageshi ni ikou

00:22:48.130 --> 00:22:53.920
Hajimete hiraku tobira sotto nozokeba

00:22:53.920 --> 00:23:01.460
Dokidoki ga tsunaideku takusan no egao

00:23:02.130 --> 00:23:09.040
Atarashii deai marugoto tsumekonde

00:23:09.040 --> 00:23:14.250
Majiwaru tabi umarete kuru harmony

00:23:14.420 --> 00:23:21.290
Shinjitetai donna kanousei mo

00:23:21.290 --> 00:23:29.380
Kono sora ga asu mo mata harewataru you ni

